":"PROSE Award for U.S. History","slug":"prose-award-for-u-s-history"},"statusLabel":"Honorable mention"}],"imprint":"Oxford University Press","publisher":"Oxford University Press","stats":{"bookId":"book-greater-gotham-a-history-of-new-york-city-from-1898-to-1919-mike-wallace","wins":1,"lists":2,"score":4,"majorWins":0,"normalWins":1,"majorShortlists":0,"normalShortlists":0,"majorLonglists":0,"normalLonglists":0,"statuses":{"winner":1,"co_winner":0,"finalist":0,"shortlist":0,"longlist":0,"honorable_mention":1,"commended":0,"notable":0,"unknown":0}},"wikipediaEvidence":{"bookId":"book-greater-gotham-a-history-of-new-york-city-from-1898-to-1919-mike-wallace","pageTitle":"Greater Gotham","pageId":83021639,"wikidataId":"Q140133796","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_Gotham","revisionId":1355766662,"accessedAt":"2026-07-14T18:47:57.494Z","extract":"Greater Gotham: A History of New York City from 1898 to 1919 is a 2017 non-fiction book by Mike Wallace. It is a comprehensive history of the city from the time of the consolidation of its five boroughs through the end of World War I. The book is the follow-up volume to the Pulitzer Prize-winning Gotham: A History of New York City to 1898, written by Wallace and Edwin G. Burrows. Though only slightly shorter than its predecessor, it covers significantly less time than the first volume due to an increase in published scholarship about the period as well as research being made easier due to the digitization of many archives. The book is separated into five sections, and in each Wallace approaches his subject from viewpoints of varying scopes. He begins with a global view of New York City's emerging power on an international scale, and gradually narrows to a microcosmic view of the city's individual residents and their daily lives. Wallace presents profiles of many New Yorkers, from the elite financiers attempting to reshape the city in their image, to the less fortunate denizens and those who advocated on their behalf. Greater Gotham was generally well received by critics, who often felt the book matched the achievement of Wallace and Burrows' first volume. It was listed on The New York Times list of 100 notable books of 2017. Some critics admired Wallace's skill at synthesizing a vast amount of source material into a single narrative, as well as his ability to write well about individual people alongside macroeconomic concepts. Some felt that even with the book's considerable size, it was lacking information on certain topics.","matchedBy":"infobox_book:high","confidence":"high","attribution":{"label":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_Gotham","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"},"infobox":{"title":"Greater Gotham: A History of New York City from 1898 to 1919","author":"Mike Wallace","publisher":"Oxford University Press","publicationDate":"2017","publicationPlace":"United States","pages":"1196 pages","isbn":"9780195116359","language":"English","subject":"History of New York City"},"publisherEvidenceId":"publisher-evidence-wikipedia-greater-gotham-a-history-of-new-york-city-from-1898-to-1919-mike-wallace"},"sources":[{"id":"source-award-record-pbk-emerson-phi-beta-kappa-ralph-waldo-emerson-award-winners","label":"Phi Beta Kappa Ralph Waldo Emerson Award winners","url":"https://www.pbk.org/awards/bookawards/emerson-winners","accessedAt":"2026-07-30T20:00:35.708Z","confidence":"official","field":"award","note":"Official awards URL: https://www.pbk.org/awards/bookawards"},{"id":"source-award-record-prose-u-s-history-prose-awards-2018-winners-archive","label":"PROSE Awards 2018 winners archive","url":"https://proseawards.com/winners/2018-award-winners/","accessedAt":"2026-07-30T20:00:35.708Z","confidence":"official","field":"award","note":"Official awards URL: https://proseawards.com/winners/2018-award-winners/"},{"id":"source-cover-google-books-greater-gotham-a-history-of-new-york-city-from-1898-to-1919-mike-wall